# BUILD FLOW 07.03 — backend/api-examples.http
# First introduced: Phase 07
# Purpose: Ready-to-send example requests for the product API, written for the REST Client extension for VS Code (other
#          .http clients understand the requests, but may not support the {{createProduct.response...}} references).
# Depends on: The backend running with the dev profile on 127.0.0.1:24081 (README "Quick start").
# Used by: Developers trying the API by hand. Runtime role: none; a request is sent only when you choose to send it.
#
# Requests are separated by lines starting with ###. Send them from top to bottom: the requests after "Create" use the
# id and version that "Create" returned. Creating twice without deleting gives 409 (the SKU is taken); delete first or
# change the SKU. Writes need the dev profile; a production deployment answers them with 403 writes-disabled.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:24081/api/v1/products

# BUILD FLOW 07.03.01 — Search

### Search: in-stock bags up to ₹3,000, cheapest first, 12 per page
GET {{baseUrl}}?category=BAGS&maxPrice=3000&inStock=true&sort=price_asc&size=12

### Search: names containing "linen" (case and accents are ignored), A to Z
GET {{baseUrl}}?q=linen&sort=name_asc

### Search: the second page of 10, newest first (pages are zero-based)
GET {{baseUrl}}?page=1&size=10

### Search with invalid parameters: 400 validation-failed listing "maxPrice" and "size"
GET {{baseUrl}}?size=500&minPrice=5000&maxPrice=1000

### Create a product: 201 Created with a Location header
# BUILD FLOW 07.03.02 — One product from creation to deletion
# (Comments go before a request line: after the blank line that ends the headers, every line is request body.)
# @name createProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "FRM-HOM-201",
  "name": "Hand-thrown Planter",
  "description": "Stoneware planter with a drainage hole and a matching saucer.",
  "category": "HOME",
  "price": 1890,
  "stockQuantity": 12,
  "imageUrl": null
}

### Read it back
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}

### Update it: the complete product plus the version you read. 200, and the version goes up by one
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "FRM-HOM-201",
  "name": "Hand-thrown Planter, Large",
  "description": "Stoneware planter with a drainage hole and a matching saucer.",
  "category": "HOME",
  "price": 2190,
  "stockQuantity": 9,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "version": {{createProduct.response.body.$.version}}
}

### The same update again: its version is now outdated, so 409 version-conflict
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "FRM-HOM-201",
  "name": "Hand-thrown Planter, Large",
  "description": "Stoneware planter with a drainage hole and a matching saucer.",
  "category": "HOME",
  "price": 2190,
  "stockQuantity": 9,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "version": {{createProduct.response.body.$.version}}
}

### Delete it: 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}

### Read it again: 404 product-not-found
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}
